  "mechanical_diagnosis": {
    "raphael": "Interaction-assisted threat conversion. Raphael does not need an earlier creature clock than Shredder to finish just as quickly; in Krang losses Raphael's first creature is later, but Raphael casts materially more interaction and wins are associated with Tough Turtle, Manhole Missile, Ninja Destroyer, and Null Group. Generic extra material does not disrupt this sequence.",
    "shredder": "Board-contestable creature progression into higher-impact closers. Shredder establishes creatures much earlier, while Krang often reaches comparable raw board counts by turns 5-7. Shredder wins are associated with Foot Mystic, Shark Shredder, Shredder Unrelenting, and Super Shredder. Proactive artifact material can alter combat/trading in some of these games, producing a modest response.",
    "answer_to_primary_question": "Additional early/proactive material helps Shredder modestly because that matchup exposes a board-combat conversion point that extra bodies or power can contest. Raphael's loss signature is not primarily missing raw board material; its interaction-backed threat conversion remains intact, so the same material does not move the matchup."
  },
